  "id": "specific-ability",
  "term": "specific ability",
  "definition": "A specific ability is a cognitive skill in which people differ that is relatively independent of general intelligence, meaning it shows little correlation with g. It refers to being especially good or poor at a particular kind of mental task rather than to broad overall mental ability.",
